# FTESurf Patch 205 -- the portal aperture.
#
# A unit quad standing in the model's YZ plane, facing +X.  Source's
# linked_portal_door is a POINT entity: it has an origin, angles and a
# width x height, and no brush anywhere in the BSP.  So the surface the
# recursed view is drawn through has to be shipped rather than found, and this
# is it.  cl_portal.qc scales it per door by handing the renderer non-unit
# axis rows (RF_USEAXIS), which is why one file serves all 443 doors in the
# library at every size from 24x56 to 1000x1000.
#
# THREE THINGS HERE ARE LOAD-BEARING AND MUST NOT BE "TIDIED":
#
# 1. The normal is exactly "1 0 0".  GLR_DrawPortal (gl_rmain.c:1133-1147)
#    takes the portal plane's normal from normals_array[0] rotated by the
#    entity's axis, and with a model normal of exactly (1,0,0) that product
#    collapses to axis[0] -- the door's own forward vector, unit length,
#    exactly the plane the physics crosses.  Any other value and the render
#    plane and the collision plane disagree.  This is also why the model is
#    .obj and not .md3: MD3 stores normals as two bytes of spherical angle,
#    and (1,0,0) quantises to (0.99998, 0, -0.00615) -- a plane tilted about
#    0.35 degrees, which over a 500-unit aperture is three units of error.
#
# 2. The four vertices are SYMMETRIC in y and z.  mod_obj_orientation defaults
#    to 1, which swaps a vertex's y and z on load (com_mesh.c:11592-11607).
#    For {(0,-1,-1),(0,1,-1),(0,1,1),(0,-1,1)} that swap is a permutation of
#    the same four points, so the quad loads identically at orientation 0 and
#    1 -- and the normal, having nothing in y or z, survives both.  (Setting
#    mod_obj_orientation 2 WOULD break it: zxy sends the normal to (0,1,0).
#    Nothing in this game needs that setting; noted so the failure is
#    recognisable rather than mysterious.)
#
# 3. The usemtl line is not decoration.  Mod_LoadObjModel copies the material
#    name into the surface's one skinframe (com_mesh.c:11773-11774), and a
#    surface whose skin does not resolve to a shader is dropped in
#    R_GAlias_DrawBatch BEFORE .forceshader is ever consulted.  The name has
#    to match the block in scripts/portal.shader.

usemtl ftesurf_portal

v 0 -1 -1
v 0  1 -1
v 0  1  1
v 0 -1  1

vt 0 0
vt 1 0
vt 1 1
vt 0 1

vn 1 0 0

f 1/1/1 2/2/1 3/3/1 4/4/1
